<h1>Open Source Group Management Software</h1>

<%= render "definition" %>

<p class="lead">GatherPack is open source group management software — MIT licensed, self-hostable, and built in the open at <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GatherPack/gatherpack</a>. Self-hosted club management stays free and yours to modify; managed hosting is there when you’d rather not run servers.</p>

<img src="/images/logo-cover.svg" alt="GatherPack open source — self-host free under MIT license" width="820" height="312" loading="lazy" style="width:100%;max-width:560px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;" class="rounded border">

<section id="why-open" class="card" aria-labelledby="why-open-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="why-open-heading">Why open source matters here</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>Many team tools are SaaS-only: your data lives in someone else’s account and leaves when you leave. GatherPack takes the opposite stance. The <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT license</a> (SPDX: <code>MIT</code>) means you can use, modify, and self-host the exact same software without a gate. That matters for volunteer-led groups where budget is tight and trust is personal — parents, churches, and nonprofits shouldn’t have to trade ownership for convenience.</p>
    <p>GatherPack grew from a <a href="https://westside-robotics.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FIRST Robotics</a> organization’s day-to-day operations. Keeping it open keeps it portable: if Sledgehammer Infosystems ever stops hosting you, the source and your data still belong to you.</p>
    <p class="mb-0"><a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View on GitHub →</a> · <a href="/hosting/">Compare hosting tiers →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="self-host" class="card" aria-labelledby="self-host-heading">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h2 id="self-host-heading">Self-host free</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>Prefer control, privacy, and zero subscription? Run GatherPack on your own server at no license cost.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>What you get:</strong> Full source, same features as hosted — <a href="/features/members/">members</a>, <a href="/features/events/">events &amp; time tracking</a>, <a href="/features/finance/">finance with Stripe</a>, <a href="/features/communication/">announcements</a>, <a href="/features/automation/">custom reports</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>What you handle:</strong> Server, updates, backups, and payment integrations (e.g., Stripe setup). Docs and community via <a href="https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> and <a href="https://discord.gg/r3fmNDVn3N" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Quick start:</strong> Clone <code>https://github.com/GatherPack/gatherpack</code>, follow the README setup. No feature gates — the MIT build is the GatherPack build.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-0 small text-muted">Alias: <code>/self-hosting</code> → canonical <code>/open-source</code>. Bookmark the canonical.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="managed" class="card" aria-labelledby="managed-heading">
